[131.780706, "i", "rotated shards.\n2. Fsync the index directory, then record each shard's committed byte length.\n3. Write and fsync a temporary checkpoint, atomically replace the checkpoint, and\n   fsync its directory.\n\nOn every resume, files outside the checkpoint are removed and longer shard files\nare truncated to their committed byte lengths before any new rows are appended.\nThis rolls back writes interrupted before checkpoint publication, including partial\nJSON/UTF-8 lines. Missing or short committed files are an error, not a reason to\nsilently skip documents. A checkpoint from the old, unsafe format triggers a\none-time rebuild because its buffered rows may never have reached disk.\n\nSIGTERM, SIGINT, and SIGHUP request a stop between documents. Completed documents\nin the partial batch are committed before exiting (75 means incomplete). SIGKILL\nrequires no cleanup: the next invocation recovers the last committed prefix.\nKeep running `./jobs reindex` after exit 75 until it returns 0. Supervisor budgets\nand transformation/check"]
[131.780712, "o", "buffer and fsync every touched shard, including rotated shards.\r\n2. Fsync the index directory, then record each shard's committed byte length.\r\n3. Write and fsync a temporary checkpoint, atomically replace the checkpoint, and\r\n   fsync its directory.\r\n\r\nOn every resume, files outside the checkpoint are removed and longer shard files\r\nare truncated to their committed byte lengths before any new rows are appended.\r\nThis rolls back writes interrupted before checkpoint publication, including partial\r\nJSON/UTF-8 lines. Missing or short committed files are an error, not a reason to\r\nsilently skip documents. A checkpoint from the old, unsafe format triggers a\r\none-time rebuild because its buffered rows may never have reached disk.\r\n\r\nSIGTERM, SIGINT, and SIGHUP request a stop between documents. Completed documents\r\nin the partial batch are committed before exiting (75 means incomplete). SIGKILL\r\nrequires no cleanup: the next invocation recovers the last committed prefix.\r\nKeep running `./jobs reindex` after exit 75 "]
[131.780728, "i", "sum/minhash semantics are unchanged. To intentionally\nrebuild after changing the corpus, use `./jobs clean` with no job running.\nEOF\n./jobs test > var/test-results.log 2>&1; cat var/test-results.log\n"]
